MODULE EXPLANATION

1. main.py

This is the central controller of the entire system.

Responsibilities:

• Starts all modules
• Captures webcam frames
• Runs the gesture detection loop
• Sends gestures to the cursor controller
• Runs voice assistant listener
• Handles system shutdown

It acts as the "brain" of the system.

---

2. hand_tracking.py

Uses MediaPipe to detect hands from the webcam.

Features:

• Detects up to 2 hands
• Tracks 21 hand landmarks
• Provides coordinates of fingers and palm

Output:

Hand landmarks used by the gesture recognition module.

---

3. gesture_recognition.py

This module analyzes hand landmarks and determines the gesture.

Supported gestures implemented:

POINT
TWO_FINGER
CLOSED_FIST
THUMB_UP
THUMB_DOWN

Each gesture returns a GestureType and additional metadata.

Example:

GestureType.TWO_FINGER
{ "scroll_y": value, "hand": "Right" }

---

4. cursor_controller.py

Controls the system mouse using gestures.

Implemented features:

Cursor movement
Mouse click
Scrolling
Cursor activation
Cursor deactivation

Gestures mapping:

POINT → move cursor
CLOSED_FIST → mouse click
TWO_FINGER → scrolling
THUMB_UP → activate cursor
THUMB_DOWN → deactivate cursor

Scrolling system was upgraded to behave like an Apple trackpad.

---

